# SLY patch tool: smart reset that only restores the files touched by conflicting
# patches, then applies all 17 over the freshly re-baselined tree. "Smart" means
# it picks the cheapest available source: local git 24.0.1 > auto-download from
# github.com (cached at documents/slycustom/downloads/) > optional user upload.
SlyPatchResetConflictFilesAndApply=Reset conflicting files + apply all
# The line of hint text shown right under the red reset button.
SlyPatchResetAllFailed=Bulk reset failed: see the FAILED lines in the log above.

# Per-row action buttons (one form per patch row in the table).
SlyPatchActions=Actions
SlyPatchApplyOne=Apply
SlyPatchResetOne=Reset
SlyPatchRestoreOne=Restore
SlyPatchApplyOneConfirmText=Apply %s to your DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT now? (Backs up every touched file first; logs at the top of the page after redirect.)
SlyPatchResetOneConfirmText=Restore %s from its per-patch backup and re-apply? (Local copy only — no network/git. The per-patch backup was created on the first successful apply.)
SlyPatchResetLocalFailed=No per-patch backup exists for: %s — local rollback is unavailable. Per-patch backups are only created by slycustom ≥ 2.2.2 on the first successful Apply of each patch. Recovery paths: (1) re-Apply on a clean 24.0.1 tree to rebuild the backup; (2) copy the missing per-patch backup directories from prod to documents/slycustom/patch-backups/per-patch/<name>/; (3) fresh git clone of official 24.0.1, re-enable slycustom, and Apply the affected patches once to populate the backups.
SlyPatchResetConflictConfirmText=Restore every file touched by the conflicting patches from its per-patch backup (every other file stays untouched), then re-Apply all 17 patches. Continue?
SlyPatchRestoreOneConfirmText=Restore %s from its per-patch backup? (Stops there — does not re-apply. After this the row shows "not applied".)
SlyPatchPerRowHint=Each row has its own Apply / Reset / Restore buttons. Reset rolls back only that one patch (using its per-patch backup) and re-applies; Restore just copies the backup back without re-applying; Apply runs a clean forward apply.
SlyPatchActionApplyAll=Apply all patches
SlyPatchActionApplyAllHint=Forward-apply the sly24.0-* series in dependency order. Every touched file is auto-backed up into the per-patch backup + pack layer. A pre-applyall bundle snapshot is taken first.
SlyPatchActionCreateBundle=Create bundle
SlyPatchActionCreateBundleHint=Snapshot the union of all 17 patch targets into one tar.gz. Use as a manual restore point before risky drift edits.
SlyPatchActionRestoreBundle=Restore from bundle
SlyPatchActionRestoreBundleHint=One-tar.gz rollback to the pre-applyall state. Resolves cross-patch overlap (per-patch restore yields a wrong intermediate state for files touched by more than one patch).
SlyPatchActionResetConflict=Reset conflicting files + apply all
SlyPatchActionResetConflictHint=For status=Conflict patches: restore their target files from the per-patch backup, then re-Apply all 17. Every other file stays untouched.
SlyPatchActionUploadBundle=Upload bundle tar.gz (recovery path)
SlyPatchActionUploadBundleHint=Last-resort recovery for conflict states. Build a clean 24.0.1 tar.gz off-host from the target list below, then upload it — the tool extracts, copies into htdocs, and (re)seeds per-patch backups: existing backup files are overwritten with the uploaded content. No network, no git, no download.
SlyPatchDownloadTargetList=Download target file list
